as of nh3 you can start a game in explore-mode (a subset of wizard mode) using
the "-X" switch (i.e. nethack -X). if you've started a normal game you can move
it to explore-mode by saving it as such (the game asks about this during save).
while in explore-mode you can cheat death, at will! but the price you pay is
that your progress does not show up on the scoreboard. you cannot move an
explore-mode game to the normal-mode, obviously.

there seems to be a need for more info for novice players. perhaps the oracles
and other humans will have a greater voice in future versions of the game. i
don't think there is any problem in giving away info but don't give away
tactics a/o strategy. not everyone has access to the source code or for that
matter cares to or is capable of reading it. that nh3 is hard should remain
a feature of the game. let trepid delvers beware ... but not ignorant.

could future versions allow the choice of pet type? perhaps thru an option
in the enviroment variables. something like:
pettype:dog    - fixes your pet to be a dog
pettype:cat    - same for cats
pettype:random - if you don't care if it's dog or cat. this is the default
                 which is assumed if the option isn't mentioned.
pettype:none   - if you really don't want a pet (some think they don't).
                 maybe they could get rewarded with a tripe ration added
                 to their starting inventory.
difficulty levels and the like have been mentioned. there's already an
explore-mode (nh3) where you can try all those ideas that you don't to risk
while playing a real game. i think the dungeon should be a common dungeon for
all players but ... maybe you could swing a deal along these lines: the game
already asks if you're experienced (in terms of character classes). it could
go one step further and ask "how experienced are you?" with the proviso that
you lose 100,000 points from your score for every experience level above 1
that you request to start the game. you want to enter the dungeon as a level
10 Samurai, you give up 0.9 Meg in score. under such a scheme i think the
players who enter the dungeon in the default manner will get the best scores
and the players who want a boost can get it at a price.
just curious: if you don't read the code or this bb how do you find out
     about Stormbringer?

